        "answer": {
          "short": "$y$: $9,\\ 4,\\ 1,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 4,\\ 9$.\n\nCoordinates: $(-3,9),\\ (-2,4),\\ (-1,1),\\ (0,0),\\ (1,1),\\ (2,4),\\ (3,9)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y(-3)&=(-3)^2=9\\\\y(-2)&=(-2)^2=4\\\\y(-1)&=(-1)^2=1\\\\y(0)&=0^2=0\\\\y(1)&=1^2=1\\\\y(2)&=2^2=4\\\\y(3)&=3^2=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe coordinates are $(-3,9),\\ (-2,4),\\ (-1,1),\\ (0,0),\\ (1,1),\\ (2,4),\\ (3,9)$. Plot each ordered pair using the horizontal coordinate first and the vertical coordinate second. The seven points do not lie on a straight line.",
