        "answer": {
          "short": "$y$: $9,\\ 4,\\ 1,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 4,\\ 9$.\n\nCoordinates: $(-2,9),\\ (-1,4),\\ (0,1),\\ (1,0),\\ (2,1),\\ (3,4),\\ (4,9)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y(-2)&=(1-(-2))^2=3^2=9\\\\y(-1)&=(1-(-1))^2=2^2=4\\\\y(0)&=(1-0)^2=1\\\\y(1)&=(1-1)^2=0\\\\y(2)&=(1-2)^2=(-1)^2=1\\\\y(3)&=(1-3)^2=(-2)^2=4\\\\y(4)&=(1-4)^2=(-3)^2=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe coordinates are $(-2,9),\\ (-1,4),\\ (0,1),\\ (1,0),\\ (2,1),\\ (3,4),\\ (4,9)$. Plot each ordered pair using the horizontal coordinate first and the vertical coordinate second. The seven points do not lie on a straight line.",
